"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"detail"},{"text":" is 0 then it will only match handlers that were connected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"without detail.  If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"detail"},{"type":"text","text":" is non-zero then it will match handlers"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connected both without detail and with the given detail.  This is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consistent with how a signal emitted with "},{"code":"detail","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" would be delivered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to those handlers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since 2.46 this also checks for a non-default class closure being"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"installed, as this is basically always what you want.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"One example of when you might use this is when the arguments to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"signal are difficult to compute. A class implementor may opt to not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"emit the signal if no one is attached anyway, thus saving the cost","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"of building the arguments.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/InitiallyUnownedRef\/signalHasHandlerPending(signalID:detail:mayBeBlocked:)"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject","doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/InitiallyUnownedRef","doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/InitiallyUnownedRef\/ObjectProtocol-Implementations"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Returns whether there are any handlers connected to ","